   "hypothesis_id": "H1",
   "mechanism": "APOE binds to the TREM2 receptor on the surface of mature microglia, facilitating lipid transport and amyloid beta uptake. This binding activates downstream PLCG2 signaling, which produces second messengers essential for microglial phagocytic responses. Genetic variants that impair this APOE-TREM2-PLCG2 axis compromise the ability of microglia to clear amyloid plaques, contributing to Alzheimer disease pathogenesis.",
   "support": "speculative",
   "supporting_evidence": [],
   "title": "APOE activates TREM2-PLCG2 signaling to promote microglial phagocytosis"
